    "notes": [
      "Measured light neutrals read near-neutral with a slight cool bias in the blue channel (canvas #DDE0E5, frame #E0E3E8, surface #E0E3E8). D-01 characterizes the frame as light warm-gray with an olive undertone; in the measured frame family the green channel sits at or a few steps above red, which is consistent with a weak olive (yellow-green) undertone but not with a warm red-leaning gray. Owner to adjudicate the D-01 characterization (UI-SPEC sec 1.4).",
      "frame, surface and surfaceMuted all measure #E0E3E8 in the timeline primary: the reference separates cards from the field by shadow, not by fill (UI-SPEC sec 10.2). The three tokens are deliberately identical at this sampling resolution; canvas is the distinct outer page field (#DDE0E5).",
      "textPrimary is frozen from the large flat dark neutral of the timeline scrubber viewport window and the MRI event-card overlay (both documented textPrimary scrims, UI-SPEC sec 6 / sec 10.2). The reference's primary ink is #000000 with 3px glyph strokes: every '72' numeral window fails the 4x4 sub-scan and the +/-4px agreement gates, and D-06 forbids freezing #000000. The rejected numeral windows are recorded in provenance.rejectedWindows.",
      "frameForeground and textSecondary are ink/background blends and are flagged visionEstimate + ownerConfirm. The reference's icon strokes and label glyphs are 2-3 px wide at this resolution, so no 8-24px window can sit wholly inside the ink; the frozen values are the darkest windows that satisfy the +/-4px agreement gate. Directional ink evidence measured in this run: frameForeground stroke cores ~#828385-#858787; textSecondary label cores ~#848689-#8A8B8E; muted axis (month) labels ~#A1A3A7. UI-SPEC provisional values were #1F232B and #8A8F98. Owner must adjudicate.",
      "critical: the Critical Alerts panel's saturated salmon members are below the minimum 8px square window. The alert-triangle icon cores (#ED4D41) and the row-1 alert avatar tint (#FEB0AF) fail the sub-scan and/or the +/-4px gates; their measurements are recorded in provenance.rejectedWindows. The frozen value (#FFCBC8) is the panel's most saturated salmon tone that satisfies the gates, so it sits close to the panel fill - the plan's 'do not freeze a soft fill' instruction could not be satisfied inside the window discipline. Owner decision required: adopt a saturated alternative from the recorded candidates, or accept the fill tone.",
      "warning is frozen from the saturated amber of the follow-up status track (the amber bar running through the Follow-up pill in the provider-home folder grid, row 1). The pill fill itself measures a pale cream #FEEDC5 and the Follow-up label text measures ~#D89830; the amber that signals Follow-up measures #FFC30C, which is close to the provider CTA gold (#FFCE03) - owner to adjudicate the warning/accent separation (D-04).",
      "borderSubtle is frozen from the horizontal timeline axis hairline (#A2A4AA). The lighter month-divider hairlines in the same reference measure #D9DBE1 on the flank column and #C6C8CE at the core, and the UI-SPEC provisional was #D8DBE1. Owner to adjudicate which hairline weight borderSubtle should carry; a light divider variant would need a second token.",
      "success is sampled from the patient-home soft mint family (the quick-log mint chips plus the Blood Glucose normal-range band). Note that the reference's semantic Normal status green lives in the provider-home folder status bars (#21AB5B saturated end, #A2E0B6 light end); the plan binds success and info to the patient-home primary.",
      "info is sampled from the patient-home lavender-blue quick-log chip (#BDCDEF). The Blood Glucose normal-range markers are the same family but are ~15px across and cannot host a conforming window.",
      "docs/reference/patient-tracking-dashboard.jpg was never sampled (D-01, D-12); it is listed in provenance.excludedAssets."
    ]
